              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "Because *Miraculous: Tales of Ladybug & Cat Noir* has notoriously inconsistent broadcasting schedules across different countries and streaming platforms, Season 2, Episode 12 refers to a few different episodes depending on the order you are following. \n\nSince Season 2 has already completely aired worldwide, **these episodes have already been released and are fully available to watch**. \n\nThe specific release dates depend on the viewing order:\n\n### 1. Production Order / Chronological Order\n* **Episode 12:** **\"Sapotis\"** (Production code: 212)\n* **Original Release Date:** **January 21, 2018** (First premiered in France on TF1/TFOU). \n* **Plot:** Alya\u2019s younger twin sisters, Ella and Etta, get akumatized into multiplying monsters called Sapotis. This episode is highly notable as it's the debut of Rena Rouge.\n\n### 2. Alternative TV/Broadcasting Orders (such as Netflix or certain TV Guides)\nDepending on the country or TV channel, Episode 12 of Season 2 is listed differently:\n* **\"Gorizilla\"** (Production code: 210)\n  * **Original Release Date:** **March 14, 2018** (First premiered in Canada on the Family Channel).\n* **\"Captain Hardrock\"** (Production code: 216)\n  * **Original Release Date:** **March 30, 2018** (First premiered in the US on Netflix). This is the episode that introduces Luka Couffaine.\n\nAll of these episodes are currently available to stream on platforms like **Disney+** and **Netflix** (depending on your region), as well as on the official Miraculous Ladybug YouTube channel.",
